---
import BaseLayout from '@chassis-ui/docs/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

// Keep this page in step with what the sites load. See ref/VERCEL_CONFIG.md for the hosts
// in the content security policy, and `Consent.astro` in the package for analytics.
const updated = '29 September 2026'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What the Chassis sites collect, why, and what you can do about it."
>
  <section class="py-3xl md:py-6xl">
    <div class="container 2xl">
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="col-span-full lg:col-span-10 lg:col-start-2 xl:col-span-8 xl:col-start-3">
          <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
          <p class="fg-subtle">Last updated {updated}.</p>

          <p>
            This notice covers chassis-ui.com and the documentation of the Chassis projects it
            serves: tokens, CSS, icons, assets, Figma and React. Chassis UI is responsible for them.
            For any question or request about your data, write to{' '}
            <a href="mailto:support@chassis-ui.com">support@chassis-ui.com</a>.
          </p>

          <h2 class="h4 mt-xl mb-xs">Analytics</h2>
          <p>
            With your consent, the sites use Google Analytics to count visits and see which pages
            are read. Nothing is sent to Google, and no analytics cookie is set, until you accept in
            the banner. Google Analytics then sets two cookies whose names start with _ga. They keep
            a random identifier for up to two years, and sends Google the pages you visit, your
            browser, your device type and your approximate location. Google does not store your IP
            address. The data is kept for two months and then deleted. Google may process it in the
            United States, under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework.
          </p>
          <p>
            Your choice is kept in your browser and covers all the Chassis sites. You can change it
            at any time with "Cookie settings" at the bottom of every page. Declining removes the
            analytics cookies.
          </p>
          <p hidden data-consent-open>
            <button type="button" class="button default">
              Cookie settings
            </button>
          </p>

          <h2 class="h4 mt-xl mb-xs">Contact form</h2>
          <p>
            When you send the form on the home page, we receive your name, your email address, your
            company if you give it, and the topic you choose. They reach us by email through our
            email provider, Resend, and are used only to answer you. We keep the message as long as
            the conversation needs it, and do not add your address to any list.
          </p>

          <h2 class="h4 mt-xl mb-xs">Fonts</h2>
          <p>
            The pages load their fonts from Google Fonts. Your browser requests them from Google's
            servers, which see your IP address and your browser, as with any request. Google Fonts
            sets no cookies.
          </p>

          <h2 class="h4 mt-xl mb-xs">Hosting</h2>
          <p>
            The sites are hosted by Vercel. To serve and protect them, Vercel handles your IP
            address and the details of each request, and keeps request logs for a short time. The
            contact form counts requests per IP address to stop abuse.
          </p>

          <h2 class="h4 mt-xl mb-xs">Stored in your browser</h2>
          <p>
            Besides the analytics cookies above, the sites keep two settings in your browser's local
            storage: your colour theme and your analytics choice. They never leave your browser.
          </p>

          <h2 class="h4 mt-xl mb-xs">Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            You can ask what we hold about you, and ask us to correct or delete it. You can withdraw
            your analytics consent at any time, without affecting what was collected before.
            Analytics rests on your consent. The contact form rests on your request to be answered.
            Hosting and fonts rest on our interest in running the sites. If you think we handle your
            data wrongly, you can complain to the data protection authority where you live.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
